   1967  fbce							; Cross-bank call pads — 2026-10-20 (chunk 4): SPLIT across the banks, no
   1968  fbce							; twin. kernel.asm holds the eleven `sta $1FFx` halves compactly at
   1969  fbce							; $FBFC..$FC1C; after the switch the fetch at A+3 lands HERE, so this bank
   1970  fbce							; keeps only the `jmp` halves (at A+3, i.e. $FBFF onward). The reverse halves
   1971  fbce							; were dead bytes: no bank1/bank2/bank3 code calls a CallPad (guard:
   1972  fbce							; verify_build.check_callpads rejects any `jsr/jmp CallPad_*` outside
   1973  fbce							; kernel.asm). F6 hotspot ignores the written value, so a pad still passes
   1974  fbce							; A/X/Y/flags through untouched (`sta` affects no flag).
